   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Tiny Planet\n\nA seeded flat skyline bends into a tiny planet through a polar remap, then keeps turning beside a red sun.\n\nCategory: camera. Length: 3.333 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A story about a city, a community or a global product needs a playful world-building beat.\n- An opener should turn an ordinary flat scene into something surprising in about a second.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The city should rise out of a grid tile by tile instead of bending: use isometric-build.\n- You want a calm cinematic landscape with depth, not a stylized planet: use parallax-depth.\n\nVariables:\n- buildings (number, 4-60): Buildings, default 26\n- seed (number, 1-99): Seed, default 4\n- spin (number, -3-3): Spin, default 0.7\n- sky_color (color): Sky, default \"#111111\"\n- ground_color (color): Ground, default \"#262626\"\n- building_color (color): Buildings, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- far_color (color): Far buildings, default \"#6B6B6B\"\n- window_color (color): Windows, default \"#111111\"\n- sun_color (color): Sun, default \"#E5322D\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
